1
00:00:01,001 --> 00:00:06,923
[theme music playing]

2
00:00:11,094 --> 00:00:14,472
[Julio] <i>We Ardientes offer</i>
<i>our condolences, Miss Aguas.</i>

3
00:00:15,181 --> 00:00:18,226
[Ivy] <i>Take me away.</i>
<i>I want to get out of this town.</i>

4
00:00:18,810 --> 00:00:20,562
<i>Arnaldo, is this yours?</i>

5
00:00:20,645 --> 00:00:22,564
<i>Yeah, that's mine.</i>
<i>I've been looking for that.</i>

6
00:00:22,647 --> 00:00:24,941
<i>-Where are you going?</i>
<i>-I'm going to look for Arthur.</i>

7
00:00:25,024 --> 00:00:27,277
<i>I'll convince him</i>
<i>to continue being a witness.</i>

8
00:00:27,360 --> 00:00:29,112
[Arthur] <i>After everything</i>
<i>I've been through</i>

9
00:00:29,195 --> 00:00:30,697
<i>at the hands of the Ardientes,</i>

10
00:00:30,780 --> 00:00:32,240
<i>I don't want to come out of hiding.</i>

11
00:00:32,323 --> 00:00:34,701
<i>I'd rather they think I'm dead.</i>

12
00:00:34,784 --> 00:00:36,077
[Raul] <i>Have dinner with me.</i>

13
00:00:36,161 --> 00:00:39,497
<i>Let's fix everything as husband and wife.</i>

14
00:00:39,581 --> 00:00:43,501
[Natalie] <i>This is the beginning</i>
<i>of your downfall, Emilia.</i>

15
00:00:43,585 --> 00:00:44,794
[Diego] <i>I won't put you in danger.</i>

16
00:00:44,878 --> 00:00:47,464
<i>I'll make sure we have enough evidence</i>

17
00:00:47,547 --> 00:00:48,923
<i>before you testify in court.</i>

18
00:00:50,216 --> 00:00:52,051
[Arthur sobbing]

19
00:00:52,135 --> 00:00:53,720
[Ivy] <i>Mr. Mayor, I want you to choose</i>

20
00:00:53,803 --> 00:00:56,598
<i>which one of these</i>
<i>I should use to kill you.</i>

21
00:00:56,681 --> 00:01:00,977
[Emilia] <i>I don't want my son</i>
<i>to end up with that bitch.</i>

22
00:01:01,061 --> 00:01:03,021
[Diego] <i>I'll follow Ivy and Arnaldo.</i>

23
00:01:03,104 --> 00:01:06,066
<i>I need to protect Ivy</i>
<i>because I don't trust Arnaldo.</i>

24
00:01:06,608 --> 00:01:09,819
[police officer] <i>She's determined</i>
<i>to catch and punish</i>

25
00:01:09,903 --> 00:01:11,488
<i>whoever murdered Carlotta.</i>

26
00:01:11,571 --> 00:01:13,114
<i>He should be careful.</i>

27
00:01:13,198 --> 00:01:15,366
<i>Miss Aguas might be planning</i>
<i>something against him.</i>

28
00:01:15,450 --> 00:01:17,077
[Arnaldo] <i>Why are you playing hard to get?</i>

29
00:01:17,160 --> 00:01:18,703
[Ivy] <i>Just don't give up.</i>

30
00:01:18,787 --> 00:01:21,748
<i>I promise you that the efforts you've made</i>

31
00:01:21,831 --> 00:01:25,126
<i>and the time you've spent waiting</i>
<i>will be worth it.</i>

32
00:01:25,210 --> 00:01:26,211
<i>Promise.</i>

33
00:01:35,178 --> 00:01:39,015
[somber music playing]

34
00:01:48,108 --> 00:01:54,614
[tense music playing]

35
00:02:04,666 --> 00:02:05,792
Hello, Aunt Camia?

36
00:02:05,875 --> 00:02:08,795
<i>Ivy and Arnaldo are currently</i>
<i>at the Ardientes' resort.</i>

37
00:02:08,878 --> 00:02:10,213
I'm on my way there.

38
00:02:10,296 --> 00:02:11,548
[Camia] <i>Be careful, Diego.</i>

39
00:02:11,631 --> 00:02:13,466
Thank you for watching over my daughter.

40
00:02:14,008 --> 00:02:15,051
Don't mention it.

41
00:02:15,593 --> 00:02:16,803
Anything for Ivy.

42
00:02:17,387 --> 00:02:18,429
Take care.

43
00:02:19,556 --> 00:02:23,351
[tense music playing]

44
00:02:32,777 --> 00:02:37,448
[engine revving]

45
00:02:40,160 --> 00:02:41,786
[engine powers down]

46
00:02:46,499 --> 00:02:48,293
[smoke hissing]

47
00:02:58,261 --> 00:02:59,429
Mister!

48
00:03:00,805 --> 00:03:02,390
-Sir?
-Is there an auto shop nearby?

49
00:03:02,473 --> 00:03:04,726
-My car broke down.
-It's a bit far from here.

50
00:03:05,059 --> 00:03:08,730
Just walk down the road,
and you'll see a small shop.

51
00:03:09,439 --> 00:03:11,399
-Okay, thank you.
-No problem, sir.

52
00:03:18,990 --> 00:03:21,367
[Julio] <i>According to our insider…</i>

53
00:03:21,868 --> 00:03:26,623
Ivy suspects there's foul play
involved in Carlotta's death.

54
00:03:27,081 --> 00:03:28,541
She never told me that.

55
00:03:28,625 --> 00:03:31,252
[Julio] <i>That's why you better</i>
<i>watch your back.</i>

56
00:03:31,544 --> 00:03:33,463
I have a feeling she's suspicious of you.

57
00:03:33,546 --> 00:03:35,924
She could be planning something.

58
00:03:36,257 --> 00:03:38,259
<i>Now, I'll get to her first.</i>

59
00:03:38,343 --> 00:03:42,889
I'll send my men over to abduct Ivy…

60
00:03:43,765 --> 00:03:46,351
and bring her to my happy place.

61
00:03:47,310 --> 00:03:48,937
<i>Whatever her plan is…</i>

62
00:03:49,020 --> 00:03:51,147
I'll squeeze it out of her brain.

63
00:03:53,066 --> 00:03:56,694
That woman is going to regret
the day she was born…

64
00:03:56,778 --> 00:03:59,989
<i>and she'll wish she was dead</i>
<i>before I get through with her.</i>

65
00:04:00,073 --> 00:04:06,621
[tense music playing]

66
00:04:08,498 --> 00:04:09,832
[Julio] <i>Arnaldo?</i>

67
00:04:09,916 --> 00:04:12,293
Arnaldo, are you still there?

68
00:04:13,169 --> 00:04:15,171
Uh, yes, Grandpa. Just a second.

69
00:04:16,756 --> 00:04:17,674
[Julio] <i>Hello?</i>

70
00:04:17,757 --> 00:04:20,260
-Is that your grandpa?
-[whispering] Yes.

71
00:04:22,637 --> 00:04:24,430
-Work?
-[whispering] Yes.

72
00:04:24,889 --> 00:04:26,599
[Ivy] Ah, work…

73
00:04:27,725 --> 00:04:30,019
We had a deal, remember?

74
00:04:31,688 --> 00:04:33,940
No work. Just…

75
00:04:34,691 --> 00:04:37,527
play all day, right?

76
00:04:39,320 --> 00:04:40,363
Fine, then.

77
00:04:42,865 --> 00:04:46,953
I'll just find someone else to play with.

78
00:04:51,874 --> 00:04:53,293
I'll just finish this.

79
00:04:55,003 --> 00:04:56,045
Hello, Grandpa?

80
00:04:56,879 --> 00:04:57,839
Hey.

81
00:04:57,922 --> 00:05:00,383
Just wait for our men, okay?

82
00:05:01,134 --> 00:05:02,302
<i>I'm telling you…</i>

83
00:05:02,385 --> 00:05:06,097
That woman will regret she lived
once I'm done making her suffer.

84
00:05:06,472 --> 00:05:07,598
There's no need for that.

85
00:05:08,641 --> 00:05:09,642
What?

86
00:05:09,726 --> 00:05:12,812
I won't let you hurt Ivy because
she's not doing anything wrong.

87
00:05:12,895 --> 00:05:13,896
[Julio] <i>What?!</i>

88
00:05:14,314 --> 00:05:15,315
How sure are you?

89
00:05:16,107 --> 00:05:17,859
I think she's starting to like me.

90
00:05:19,610 --> 00:05:21,487
Everything is falling into place,

91
00:05:21,779 --> 00:05:24,532
and it's only a matter of time
before we become a couple.

92
00:05:24,615 --> 00:05:25,533
[scoffs]

93
00:05:25,616 --> 00:05:26,784
I trust her, Grandpa.

94
00:05:27,744 --> 00:05:29,245
She'd never betray me.

95
00:05:33,416 --> 00:05:34,500
I have to go.

96
00:05:35,335 --> 00:05:40,006
[unsettling music playing]

97
00:05:42,842 --> 00:05:43,926
Are you done?

98
00:05:46,220 --> 00:05:47,722
Can you rub some lotion on me?

99
00:05:48,306 --> 00:05:49,348
Sure.

100
00:05:55,271 --> 00:05:56,355
Here.

101
00:06:13,372 --> 00:06:14,415
[moans]

102
00:06:15,333 --> 00:06:16,292
Okay, enough.

103
00:06:17,877 --> 00:06:19,212
Let's eat first.

104
00:06:19,587 --> 00:06:21,130
I have to finish that later.

105
00:06:22,131 --> 00:06:23,174
We'll see.

106
00:06:23,466 --> 00:06:25,593
Okay, let's eat!

107
00:06:26,260 --> 00:06:33,184
[upbeat music playing]

108
00:07:13,224 --> 00:07:17,478
[upbeat music playing]

109
00:07:24,110 --> 00:07:30,908
[upbeat music playing]

110
00:08:10,990 --> 00:08:12,033
Hi!

111
00:08:12,658 --> 00:08:14,952
-Can you help me?
-Yeah, sure.

112
00:08:21,292 --> 00:08:22,293
[Ivy chuckles]

113
00:08:22,376 --> 00:08:23,419
Thank you.

114
00:08:24,128 --> 00:08:30,551
[tense music playing]

115
00:08:43,648 --> 00:08:45,525
Oh! Oysters.

116
00:08:46,526 --> 00:08:47,568
All right.

117
00:08:50,571 --> 00:08:52,907
[Prianka] <i>Casanova, the greatest lover…</i>

118
00:08:53,407 --> 00:08:56,536
<i>loved eating oysters for breakfast.</i>

119
00:08:56,619 --> 00:08:59,539
<i>It was his favorite aphrodisiac.</i>

120
00:09:00,998 --> 00:09:04,544
[tense music playing]

121
00:09:09,757 --> 00:09:10,758
Want one?

122
00:09:11,133 --> 00:09:12,176
Of course.

123
00:09:15,596 --> 00:09:16,639
Cheers.

124
00:09:17,723 --> 00:09:22,895
[tense music playing]

125
00:09:24,105 --> 00:09:25,022
Yum.

126
00:09:35,908 --> 00:09:37,410
-It's cold.
-[Arnaldo chuckles]

127
00:09:37,785 --> 00:09:38,828
Here.

128
00:09:41,998 --> 00:09:43,874
-Here.
-Oh, thank you.

129
00:09:44,625 --> 00:09:45,918
I need to dry my legs.

130
00:09:46,752 --> 00:09:47,795
[sighs]

131
00:09:50,214 --> 00:09:51,257
Sorry.

132
00:09:54,844 --> 00:09:55,970
I'll get us some drinks.

133
00:09:56,679 --> 00:09:58,264
No. Stay here.

134
00:09:59,265 --> 00:10:00,308
Do it later.

135
00:10:05,771 --> 00:10:07,356
Arnaldo, stop.

136
00:10:08,149 --> 00:10:10,318
Things are happening so fast.

137
00:10:12,528 --> 00:10:15,156
Sometimes, I think
you're just leading me on.

138
00:10:15,740 --> 00:10:17,366
[sighs]

139
00:10:19,493 --> 00:10:21,078
Why would I do that?

140
00:10:21,162 --> 00:10:22,872
You're playing push-and-pull on me.

141
00:10:22,955 --> 00:10:25,124
One minute you're hot,
the next thing you're cold.

142
00:10:25,207 --> 00:10:26,834
What do you really want?
Tell me the truth.

143
00:10:26,917 --> 00:10:30,338
I already told you that
I'm not like your other girls.

144
00:10:30,421 --> 00:10:32,798
I have self-respect.

145
00:10:33,841 --> 00:10:35,760
Don't you understand that?

146
00:10:37,887 --> 00:10:38,888
[sighs]

147
00:10:41,307 --> 00:10:42,475
[sighs] Okay.

148
00:10:44,185 --> 00:10:45,353
Okay, I'm sorry.

149
00:10:50,316 --> 00:10:51,359
Arnaldo…

150
00:10:53,235 --> 00:10:55,446
I do want to give myself to you.

151
00:10:56,947 --> 00:10:59,742
But only at the right time and place.

152
00:11:06,207 --> 00:11:07,750
If you wait…

153
00:11:08,334 --> 00:11:10,044
I'm sure…

154
00:11:12,922 --> 00:11:15,257
you'll get a huge reward from me.

155
00:11:22,348 --> 00:11:23,391
All right.

156
00:11:24,183 --> 00:11:25,226
I'll wait.

157
00:11:28,521 --> 00:11:29,605
Good boy.

158
00:11:31,857 --> 00:11:33,692
-Okay, I'll get our drinks.
-No.

159
00:11:34,068 --> 00:11:35,986
No, just…

160
00:11:36,737 --> 00:11:38,239
stay here.

161
00:11:39,990 --> 00:11:41,117
I'll get it.

162
00:11:42,284 --> 00:11:43,744
Just wait for me here.

163
00:11:45,871 --> 00:11:46,747
Behave.

164
00:11:48,791 --> 00:11:49,917
Wait for me.

165
00:11:52,336 --> 00:11:53,295
[exhales]

166
00:12:01,720 --> 00:12:02,888
I'll do it.

167
00:12:02,972 --> 00:12:05,349
Just get me another bottle of wine.

168
00:12:05,433 --> 00:12:06,559
Okay, ma'am.

169
00:12:20,656 --> 00:12:22,074
[ice clinks]

170
00:12:23,367 --> 00:12:29,039
[tense music playing]

171
00:12:46,223 --> 00:12:50,394
[tense music intensifies]

172
00:13:27,932 --> 00:13:28,974
Arnaldo.

173
00:13:32,686 --> 00:13:33,729
It's enough.

174
00:13:35,523 --> 00:13:36,315
-Cheers.
-Cheers.

175
00:13:36,398 --> 00:13:37,775
[glasses clink]

176
00:13:40,736 --> 00:13:42,488
You know what? You're right.

177
00:13:43,447 --> 00:13:45,991
I'm used to dating easy women.

178
00:13:46,700 --> 00:13:48,035
Think about it, just like Natalie.

179
00:13:48,661 --> 00:13:51,747
After our first date, she was all over me.

180
00:13:51,830 --> 00:13:54,667
But what happened?
It's over. I got tired of her.

181
00:13:56,502 --> 00:13:57,628
But, with you…

182
00:13:58,921 --> 00:13:59,964
You're different.

183
00:14:00,923 --> 00:14:02,049
Arnaldo…

184
00:14:03,384 --> 00:14:06,011
I'm not just doing this for you.

185
00:14:06,637 --> 00:14:07,763
This is who I am.

186
00:14:07,846 --> 00:14:09,848
I know, and it's driving me crazy.

187
00:14:10,808 --> 00:14:16,730
[unsettling music playing]

188
00:14:19,984 --> 00:14:24,488
Arnaldo, have you been obsessed
with a woman before?

189
00:14:25,197 --> 00:14:26,740
What kind of question is that?

190
00:14:28,242 --> 00:14:29,285
Well…

191
00:14:29,743 --> 00:14:31,871
We're here now, so…

192
00:14:32,705 --> 00:14:34,456
I want to know you more.

193
00:14:35,541 --> 00:14:37,001
Okay. Well, to answer your question,

194
00:14:37,084 --> 00:14:39,628
what's the craziest thing I did
for a woman I loved?

195
00:14:41,714 --> 00:14:44,717
Maybe, it was when I beat up
my rival in college.

196
00:14:46,635 --> 00:14:47,803
That's it?

197
00:14:47,887 --> 00:14:50,681
For an Ardiente like you…

198
00:14:51,015 --> 00:14:52,308
I'm disappointed.

199
00:14:54,059 --> 00:14:56,020
Why? What did you expect me to say?

200
00:14:56,520 --> 00:14:57,563
Murder.

201
00:15:00,190 --> 00:15:01,859
People say that…

202
00:15:03,068 --> 00:15:05,529
the Ardientes are murderers.

203
00:15:07,323 --> 00:15:09,158
So, I just want to know…

204
00:15:11,035 --> 00:15:12,119
if you…

205
00:15:17,958 --> 00:15:18,959
Have you…

206
00:15:20,127 --> 00:15:21,629
Arnaldo…

207
00:15:22,630 --> 00:15:24,256
Have you killed someone…

208
00:15:25,591 --> 00:15:27,343
in the name of love?

209
00:15:33,724 --> 00:15:36,018
[screaming]

210
00:15:39,647 --> 00:15:40,898
I'm sorry to disappoint you.

211
00:15:42,232 --> 00:15:43,442
I wouldn't do that.

212
00:15:44,360 --> 00:15:45,611
I was raised differently.

213
00:15:45,694 --> 00:15:51,116
Grandpa taught me to use
my brain over my emotions.

214
00:15:51,951 --> 00:15:53,619
If you let emotions take over…

215
00:15:55,746 --> 00:15:57,081
you could end up killing someone.

216
00:15:58,791 --> 00:16:02,002
And I can't let those things happen.

217
00:16:04,380 --> 00:16:06,507
Sure. I believe you.

218
00:16:10,302 --> 00:16:12,054
-Cheers?
-Cheers.

219
00:16:19,728 --> 00:16:21,271
Is it good?

220
00:16:22,022 --> 00:16:23,148
It's perfect.

221
00:16:24,358 --> 00:16:25,734
You don't look satisfied.

222
00:16:26,527 --> 00:16:27,486
Do you want more?

223
00:16:27,569 --> 00:16:28,696
You.

224
00:16:29,738 --> 00:16:30,781
I want you.

225
00:16:32,616 --> 00:16:39,039
[melodramatic music playing]

226
00:17:06,608 --> 00:17:13,449
[tense music playing]

227
00:17:26,962 --> 00:17:28,005
[thump]

228
00:17:39,975 --> 00:17:46,982
[tense music intensifies]

229
00:17:51,570 --> 00:17:54,406
[tense music fades]

230
00:18:00,496 --> 00:18:07,503
[tense music playing]

231
00:18:22,684 --> 00:18:28,565
[tense music intensifies]

232
00:18:30,192 --> 00:18:31,527
[tense music fades]

233
00:18:40,119 --> 00:18:47,126
[tense music playing]

234
00:19:05,769 --> 00:19:09,940
<i>Your death isn't enough payment</i>
<i>for what you did.</i>

235
00:19:12,276 --> 00:19:15,362
<i>I won't let you off that easily, Arnaldo.</i>

236
00:19:15,445 --> 00:19:19,741
<i>I won't taint my hands</i>
<i>with blood for someone like you.</i>

237
00:19:19,825 --> 00:19:23,954
<i>You deserve a fate far worse than this.</i>

238
00:19:24,037 --> 00:19:30,502
[tense music intensifies]

239
00:19:33,297 --> 00:19:40,262
[melodramatic music playing]

240
00:19:57,863 --> 00:19:59,573
<i>Mark my words…</i>

241
00:19:59,656 --> 00:20:04,077
<i>You'll meet the same fate</i>
<i>as Nanny Carlotta.</i>

242
00:20:04,161 --> 00:20:10,083
<i>I'll make you suffer so much</i>
<i>you'll want to kill yourself.</i>

243
00:20:19,051 --> 00:20:21,053
<i>It won't be revenge.</i>

244
00:20:21,762 --> 00:20:22,888
<i>It'll be justice.</i>

245
00:20:28,352 --> 00:20:34,608
[tense music playing]

246
00:21:30,914 --> 00:21:32,040
Wait, Raul.

247
00:21:32,582 --> 00:21:33,583
Hold on.

248
00:21:34,042 --> 00:21:36,503
This isn't right.

249
00:21:37,337 --> 00:21:38,297
Something's off.

250
00:21:38,380 --> 00:21:39,548
[scoffs]

251
00:21:40,340 --> 00:21:42,050
What do you mean this isn't right?

252
00:21:42,342 --> 00:21:44,011
I'm your husband. You're my wife.

253
00:21:44,094 --> 00:21:46,722
There's nothing wrong with that.

254
00:21:49,474 --> 00:21:51,184
I don't know if…

255
00:21:52,769 --> 00:21:56,148
this is serious or
just another game of yours.

256
00:21:57,190 --> 00:21:58,817
-I don't want to get hurt again.
-Shh…

257
00:22:01,069 --> 00:22:02,904
Emilia, what do I have to do…

258
00:22:03,864 --> 00:22:08,160
for you to trust me
and believe that I love you?

259
00:22:08,952 --> 00:22:09,995
I'll do it.

260
00:22:10,662 --> 00:22:11,705
Just tell me.

261
00:22:15,167 --> 00:22:16,209
Kneel before me.

262
00:22:18,045 --> 00:22:19,504
Kiss my feet.

263
00:22:20,464 --> 00:22:22,299
Do you want me to ask
for your forgiveness?

264
00:22:22,841 --> 00:22:23,884
No.

265
00:22:24,968 --> 00:22:26,595
Worship me.

266
00:22:29,598 --> 00:22:35,479
[unsettling music playing]

267
00:23:00,962 --> 00:23:02,672
Raul, no…

268
00:23:06,343 --> 00:23:07,260
Emilia…

269
00:23:08,804 --> 00:23:10,138
I love you so much.

270
00:23:11,473 --> 00:23:13,016
I would worship you.

271
00:23:17,521 --> 00:23:23,360
[melodramatic music playing]

272
00:23:41,586 --> 00:23:42,963
[engine starts]

273
00:23:44,131 --> 00:23:46,341
-Is it okay?
-Yes. Turn it off.

274
00:23:49,386 --> 00:23:50,554
[engine powers down]

275
00:23:50,637 --> 00:23:53,473
It's fixed. I changed the fan belt. See?

276
00:23:54,349 --> 00:23:55,225
Thank you.

277
00:23:57,185 --> 00:23:58,520
Here's the payment.

278
00:24:00,063 --> 00:24:01,106
-Thank you.
-Mister…

279
00:24:01,189 --> 00:24:04,734
-Is La Union far from here?
-It's about an hour away.

280
00:24:04,818 --> 00:24:06,403
-All right, thank you.
-You're welcome.

281
00:24:23,795 --> 00:24:26,047
[engine revving]

282
00:24:28,508 --> 00:24:35,182
[tense music playing]

283
00:24:46,067 --> 00:24:47,110
[Ivy] Hi.

284
00:24:47,903 --> 00:24:50,197
I thought you'd never wake up.

285
00:24:53,116 --> 00:24:55,869
-What time is it?
-Almost noon.

286
00:24:55,952 --> 00:24:58,038
I see. What happened last night?

287
00:25:00,540 --> 00:25:01,791
A lot.

288
00:25:01,875 --> 00:25:05,795
Well, you drank a lot.
You were really drunk.

289
00:25:07,214 --> 00:25:10,884
[sighs] I almost left,
but I felt sorry for you.

290
00:25:13,637 --> 00:25:14,888
Ouch!

291
00:25:14,971 --> 00:25:17,057
Why am I wounded?

292
00:25:18,433 --> 00:25:20,018
Because you were too rowdy.

293
00:25:21,061 --> 00:25:23,730
You accidentally cut yourself
with a knife.

294
00:25:26,900 --> 00:25:27,943
Did…

295
00:25:28,777 --> 00:25:30,528
Did something happen
between us last night?

296
00:25:35,867 --> 00:25:36,868
What?

297
00:25:37,953 --> 00:25:39,537
Did something happen
between us last night?

298
00:25:44,584 --> 00:25:45,627
You know…

299
00:25:46,461 --> 00:25:51,132
If something does happen,
I'll make sure you remember it.

300
00:25:51,216 --> 00:25:54,803
You won't ever forget it.

301
00:25:58,223 --> 00:26:00,642
So, nothing happened.

302
00:26:01,434 --> 00:26:02,560
Maybe next time.

303
00:26:07,023 --> 00:26:08,108
Come on.

304
00:26:09,109 --> 00:26:12,070
Breakfast is ready.
I'll just see you downstairs.

305
00:26:12,988 --> 00:26:14,030
Okay.

306
00:26:15,865 --> 00:26:17,200
Good morning.

307
00:26:18,118 --> 00:26:24,833
[unsettling music playing]

308
00:26:33,883 --> 00:26:35,760
Mom, I'll be fine.

309
00:26:36,553 --> 00:26:39,097
I'm just worried that Arnaldo
will do something to you.

310
00:26:39,472 --> 00:26:41,641
If you're worried about Arnaldo…

311
00:26:41,725 --> 00:26:43,393
<i>I can take care of myself.</i>

312
00:26:43,727 --> 00:26:45,562
I'm more worried about you.

313
00:26:46,062 --> 00:26:47,605
Are you going to see the farmers today?

314
00:26:47,689 --> 00:26:48,690
Yes, dear.

315
00:26:48,773 --> 00:26:51,651
The farmers' cooperative
invited me to give a talk.

316
00:26:52,193 --> 00:26:56,156
Mom, don't go anywhere
without your bodyguards.

317
00:26:56,489 --> 00:26:57,615
You need to be careful,

318
00:26:57,699 --> 00:26:59,534
especially now that I'm out of town.

319
00:26:59,993 --> 00:27:01,119
Yes, dear.

320
00:27:01,202 --> 00:27:02,704
Be careful, Mom.

321
00:27:02,787 --> 00:27:05,123
I will, dear. Don't worry about me.

322
00:27:05,832 --> 00:27:06,875
<i>Bye.</i>

323
00:27:16,634 --> 00:27:17,677
Hi!

324
00:27:18,428 --> 00:27:20,263
-Good morning.
-Let's eat.

325
00:27:22,891 --> 00:27:23,892
Thanks.

326
00:27:25,477 --> 00:27:26,603
What do you want?

327
00:27:26,686 --> 00:27:29,814
-Maybe some coffee?
-No, this is perfect.

328
00:27:29,898 --> 00:27:31,024
You're perfect.

329
00:27:32,025 --> 00:27:33,276
Arnaldo…

330
00:27:35,820 --> 00:27:37,781
-Let's eat.
-Yeah.

331
00:27:43,244 --> 00:27:44,245
[sighs]

332
00:27:51,336 --> 00:27:52,879
Good morning!

333
00:27:53,838 --> 00:27:55,090
Hi, sexy.

334
00:27:57,258 --> 00:27:58,301
Wow!

335
00:27:59,052 --> 00:28:00,178
That looks delicious.

336
00:28:02,472 --> 00:28:05,767
Who's more delicious? The food or me?

337
00:28:07,644 --> 00:28:09,813
[chuckles] Do you have to ask that?

338
00:28:10,563 --> 00:28:11,815
Of course…

339
00:28:12,732 --> 00:28:13,775
It's you.

340
00:28:13,858 --> 00:28:16,236
You're more delicious than the food.

341
00:28:16,319 --> 00:28:17,404
[chortles]

342
00:28:17,487 --> 00:28:18,822
Good answer.

343
00:28:22,325 --> 00:28:23,743
-Raul?
-Yeah?

344
00:28:24,411 --> 00:28:26,037
Can you please slap me?

345
00:28:27,080 --> 00:28:29,582
I want to make sure I'm not dreaming

346
00:28:29,666 --> 00:28:33,336
because I still can't believe
we're finally getting along.

347
00:28:35,004 --> 00:28:36,214
No, Emilia.

348
00:28:39,384 --> 00:28:40,677
You're not dreaming.

349
00:28:43,138 --> 00:28:44,180
Come here.

350
00:28:44,973 --> 00:28:47,517
From now on, you have to get used to this.

351
00:28:48,351 --> 00:28:50,311
Things can only get better.

352
00:28:51,062 --> 00:28:52,147
[sighs]

353
00:28:53,314 --> 00:28:54,607
I love you.

354
00:29:08,747 --> 00:29:14,085
[tense music playing]

355
00:29:16,087 --> 00:29:19,632
Sir Diego! It's been a while
since you came here.

356
00:29:20,759 --> 00:29:22,510
-Is Arnaldo here?
-Yes, sir.

357
00:29:22,594 --> 00:29:24,929
He's with his guest at the rest house.

358
00:29:25,346 --> 00:29:29,142
Okay. Don't tell him I'm here.
I want to surprise him.

359
00:29:29,517 --> 00:29:30,560
Yes, sir.

360
00:29:30,894 --> 00:29:32,020
-Thank you.
-Okay, sir.

361
00:29:37,275 --> 00:29:42,238
[phone ringing]

362
00:29:43,865 --> 00:29:45,492
-Hello, Auntie?
-<i>Diego.</i>

363
00:29:45,575 --> 00:29:47,160
I've got some bad news.

364
00:29:47,243 --> 00:29:48,536
What happened?

365
00:29:48,620 --> 00:29:50,955
A typhoon hit the area.

366
00:29:51,039 --> 00:29:53,208
The co-op office was hit pretty bad.

367
00:29:53,291 --> 00:29:57,045
<i>The winds were so strong that</i>
<i>they destroyed the roof and walls.</i>

368
00:29:57,128 --> 00:29:59,339
We were able to save
some campaign materials,

369
00:29:59,422 --> 00:30:01,716
but most of them got ruined.

370
00:30:02,258 --> 00:30:04,135
I'll have it fixed when I return.

371
00:30:04,803 --> 00:30:06,179
[Loring] <i>That's good to hear.</i>

372
00:30:06,262 --> 00:30:08,348
But do we have funds?

373
00:30:09,933 --> 00:30:12,936
Don't worry about it. I'll find a way.

374
00:30:13,311 --> 00:30:14,562
That's great.

375
00:30:14,646 --> 00:30:18,775
You're a true leader indeed.
You don't give up that easily.

376
00:30:18,858 --> 00:30:20,401
[Pandoy] <i>Go, Diego! Go!</i>

377
00:30:20,485 --> 00:30:21,611
-Right, everyone?
-Go, Diego!

378
00:30:21,694 --> 00:30:22,695
Diego will help us--

379
00:30:22,779 --> 00:30:23,863
-[metal crashing]
-[screaming]

380
00:30:23,947 --> 00:30:25,782
-<i>My goodness!</i>
-What's happening there?

381
00:30:25,865 --> 00:30:28,368
-Watch out!
-Be careful!

382
00:30:28,827 --> 00:30:31,704
It's just one of the metal roof sheets.

383
00:30:31,788 --> 00:30:33,581
<i>The wind blew another one away.</i>

384
00:30:34,165 --> 00:30:36,668
I promise I'll have it fixed
when I return.

385
00:30:36,960 --> 00:30:38,044
Thanks, Diego.

386
00:30:39,254 --> 00:30:40,672
Take care of yourself, all right?

387
00:30:40,755 --> 00:30:41,548
Take care!

388
00:30:41,631 --> 00:30:43,633
I will. Be safe too.

389
00:30:54,727 --> 00:30:57,814
[water drizzling]

390
00:31:03,069 --> 00:31:09,993
[tense music playing]

391
00:31:20,336 --> 00:31:26,342
[tense music playing]

392
00:32:33,993 --> 00:32:35,328
Diego?

393
00:32:35,411 --> 00:32:37,372
I almost killed you.

394
00:32:37,914 --> 00:32:39,499
Why are you here?

395
00:32:39,999 --> 00:32:41,417
To watch over you.

396
00:32:42,502 --> 00:32:44,003
I don't trust Arnaldo.

397
00:32:44,754 --> 00:32:46,714
You'll ruin my plans.

398
00:32:47,131 --> 00:32:48,758
-Leave now.
-No.

399
00:32:49,217 --> 00:32:51,260
I'll stay here to protect you.

400
00:32:58,518 --> 00:32:59,852
[knocking on door]

401
00:32:59,936 --> 00:33:00,937
Ivy?

402
00:33:04,190 --> 00:33:05,566
Ivy, are you there?

403
00:33:06,859 --> 00:33:08,569
-[whispering] See?
-[knocking on door]

404
00:33:09,112 --> 00:33:10,238
Ivy.

405
00:33:10,321 --> 00:33:11,197
[knocking on door]

406
00:33:11,280 --> 00:33:14,367
Uh… Arnaldo, yeah! Wait a second!

407
00:33:14,450 --> 00:33:15,910
[whispering] You have to hide!

408
00:33:17,870 --> 00:33:19,580
Ivy? [knocking on door]

409
00:33:20,039 --> 00:33:21,791
[knocking continues]

410
00:33:21,874 --> 00:33:23,376
Ivy, open the door.

411
00:33:25,086 --> 00:33:26,337
I'm coming!

412
00:33:26,671 --> 00:33:28,715
[knocking on door] Ivy.

413
00:33:28,923 --> 00:33:30,049
[knocking continues]

414
00:33:30,925 --> 00:33:32,385
[knocking continues]

415
00:33:32,468 --> 00:33:33,803
-Yes, Arnaldo?
-Ivy!

416
00:33:33,886 --> 00:33:35,179
I'm coming! Hi!

417
00:33:35,263 --> 00:33:36,222
What took you so long?

418
00:33:36,305 --> 00:33:37,682
-Is there a problem?
-Um…

419
00:33:38,141 --> 00:33:39,183
Arnaldo…

420
00:33:39,892 --> 00:33:41,019
Come here.

421
00:33:42,270 --> 00:33:43,271
[Ivy moans]

422
00:33:45,231 --> 00:33:47,650
I was just changing,
that's why I took so long.

423
00:33:47,734 --> 00:33:51,404
Okay. Well, I came here because
I want you to come with me.

424
00:33:53,781 --> 00:33:55,116
-Where?
-Just come.

425
00:33:55,199 --> 00:33:57,410
I'll bring you to a special place.

426
00:33:58,661 --> 00:33:59,912
Okay? Let's go.

427
00:33:59,996 --> 00:34:01,122
All right.

428
00:34:03,249 --> 00:34:04,292
Hang on.

429
00:34:05,084 --> 00:34:09,922
[tense music playing]

430
00:34:14,802 --> 00:34:15,845
Um…

431
00:34:20,266 --> 00:34:21,309
Yeah.

432
00:34:42,622 --> 00:34:45,708
-Can we still use those?
-Yes, they're fine.

433
00:34:45,792 --> 00:34:48,252
[Loring] We need to prepare
for the meeting.

434
00:34:48,336 --> 00:34:50,004
-We need to saw this off.
-Oh, dear!

435
00:34:50,421 --> 00:34:53,091
-Let's cut this, okay?
-Miss Camia is here!

436
00:34:54,175 --> 00:34:56,260
-It's Miss Camia!
-Here she is!

437
00:34:56,344 --> 00:34:58,262
Everyone, it's Miss Camia!

438
00:34:58,346 --> 00:34:59,806
-Ma'am!
-Miss Camia.

439
00:34:59,889 --> 00:35:01,307
-Oh, no!
-Ma'am.

440
00:35:01,641 --> 00:35:03,434
Miss Loring, what happened here?

441
00:35:03,518 --> 00:35:06,145
It got destroyed by the typhoon.

442
00:35:06,521 --> 00:35:09,816
But it won't take long
for us to fix it, ma'am.

443
00:35:09,899 --> 00:35:12,985
-Please have a seat.
-Don't worry about me.

444
00:35:13,069 --> 00:35:14,779
Is there anything I can do to help?

445
00:35:14,862 --> 00:35:16,572
-No, it's fine.
-Don't worry about us.

446
00:35:16,656 --> 00:35:19,951
-We got this. Have a seat.
-Thank you, Nimfa.

447
00:35:20,034 --> 00:35:21,369
Ma'am, this won't take long.

448
00:35:21,452 --> 00:35:23,788
-We'll fix it so we can start.
-Don't worry about me.

449
00:35:23,871 --> 00:35:26,207
-Hurry up, everyone!
-I got this, Miss Loring!

450
00:35:26,290 --> 00:35:28,417
-Are you okay, ma'am?
-I'm fine, thanks.

451
00:35:28,501 --> 00:35:29,836
I'm so sorry, ma'am.

452
00:35:30,169 --> 00:35:32,004
I can wait. Don't worry about me.

453
00:35:32,088 --> 00:35:33,422
-Pandoy.
-What?

454
00:35:33,506 --> 00:35:34,841
Aren't you supposed to dry that up?

455
00:35:34,924 --> 00:35:36,050
I'm on it.

456
00:35:43,975 --> 00:35:45,017
Perfect!

457
00:35:45,643 --> 00:35:46,644
I like it.

458
00:35:48,229 --> 00:35:49,272
[chortles]

459
00:35:52,900 --> 00:35:53,943
Ew!

460
00:35:54,318 --> 00:35:55,361
Why?

461
00:35:56,445 --> 00:35:57,780
Is that Emilia's?

462
00:35:57,864 --> 00:35:59,532
-[chuckles]
-She smells old!

463
00:35:59,615 --> 00:36:00,867
[puffs and whines]

464
00:36:01,325 --> 00:36:03,077
I think you should take a shower.

465
00:36:04,579 --> 00:36:05,705
You know what, Natalie?

466
00:36:07,748 --> 00:36:10,001
Right now, I'm in control
of the situation.

467
00:36:10,626 --> 00:36:13,379
That's why I can provide you
with everything you need.

468
00:36:13,921 --> 00:36:16,340
But you have to give me what I need too

469
00:36:17,425 --> 00:36:21,929
so I can tell you everything
you want to know.

470
00:36:25,850 --> 00:36:26,893
Well…

471
00:36:27,935 --> 00:36:28,978
What do you need?

472
00:36:29,854 --> 00:36:30,897
Money?

473
00:36:33,733 --> 00:36:34,817
Guns?

474
00:36:37,320 --> 00:36:38,321
Hmm…

475
00:36:39,113 --> 00:36:40,823
An army?

476
00:36:45,995 --> 00:36:47,288
All of the above.

477
00:36:48,748 --> 00:36:51,042
I need to be stronger than the Ardientes.

478
00:36:56,797 --> 00:36:59,300
[Camia] <i>The Ardientes aren't</i>
<i>the ones keeping us</i>

479
00:36:59,383 --> 00:37:01,469
from getting the justice we deserve.

480
00:37:01,928 --> 00:37:05,806
They are not our biggest enemies, either.

481
00:37:05,890 --> 00:37:07,516
It is fear.

482
00:37:08,309 --> 00:37:11,896
Fear stops us from fighting for justice

483
00:37:11,979 --> 00:37:14,232
that the Ardientes have long withheld.

484
00:37:15,775 --> 00:37:18,110
So, we must rise above our fears!

485
00:37:18,736 --> 00:37:21,030
-That's right!
-Yes!

486
00:37:21,113 --> 00:37:25,034
They cannot oppress us if we are united!

487
00:37:25,117 --> 00:37:26,369
Miss Camia is right.

488
00:37:26,452 --> 00:37:28,621
-Long live the new Ardiente!
-[farmers] Long live!

489
00:37:28,704 --> 00:37:31,540
-Long live the new Ardiente!
-Long live!

490
00:37:31,624 --> 00:37:34,377
-Long live the new Ardiente!
-[all] Long live!

491
00:37:34,961 --> 00:37:40,383
-[applause]
-[melodramatic music playing]

492
00:37:55,439 --> 00:37:56,732
When I was a kid,

493
00:37:58,150 --> 00:38:00,653
I'd always come to this place to be alone.

494
00:38:01,696 --> 00:38:04,991
When Grandpa would look for me,
he'd know to find me here.

495
00:38:05,908 --> 00:38:07,660
It's a special place,

496
00:38:07,743 --> 00:38:10,204
and I want to share it
with a special someone,

497
00:38:10,288 --> 00:38:11,330
and that's you.

498
00:38:13,249 --> 00:38:14,333
Arnaldo…

499
00:38:22,591 --> 00:38:24,260
Arnaldo, behave!

500
00:38:26,887 --> 00:38:29,265
How long will you keep me waiting, huh?

501
00:38:30,933 --> 00:38:31,892
I'm sorry.

502
00:38:32,393 --> 00:38:35,855
I promised my parents that
I'd only give myself

503
00:38:35,938 --> 00:38:37,189
to the person I love most.

504
00:38:37,273 --> 00:38:39,025
To my future husband.

505
00:38:41,277 --> 00:38:43,863
You mean to say all this time,

506
00:38:44,655 --> 00:38:45,489
you were a virgin?

507
00:38:46,615 --> 00:38:47,533
Yes.

508
00:38:48,034 --> 00:38:49,160
Yes, Arnaldo.

509
00:38:51,203 --> 00:38:57,585
[unsettling music playing]

510
00:39:18,773 --> 00:39:25,780
[tense music playing]

511
00:39:39,126 --> 00:39:40,169
Wait.

512
00:39:45,925 --> 00:39:47,968
-[Arnaldo grunts]
-What happened?

513
00:39:48,636 --> 00:39:50,304
-Are you okay?
-I'm fine. I just tripped.

514
00:39:50,388 --> 00:39:53,474
-Look, I brought you this.
-Oh! Thank you, Arnaldo!

515
00:39:53,557 --> 00:39:55,935
I'm okay. It's just a scratch.

516
00:39:56,018 --> 00:39:58,145
We should go back to the rest house.

517
00:39:58,229 --> 00:40:00,022
-Come on.
-Okay.

518
00:40:01,774 --> 00:40:02,775
[Arnaldo sighs]

519
00:40:02,858 --> 00:40:03,943
Okay, let's go.

520
00:40:07,738 --> 00:40:09,824
-Are you sure you're okay?
-I'm okay. Really.

521
00:40:09,907 --> 00:40:11,283
-You sure?
-Yes.

522
00:40:11,367 --> 00:40:13,160
-Do you like it?
-Yeah.

523
00:40:15,538 --> 00:40:17,748
-[Arnaldo grunting]
-We're almost there.

524
00:40:19,417 --> 00:40:22,670
-Okay, sit down.
-Wait, I can do this.

525
00:40:23,921 --> 00:40:24,880
[grunts]

526
00:40:24,964 --> 00:40:28,259
Okay. Oh, wait.
I have painkillers in the car.

527
00:40:28,342 --> 00:40:31,178
Stay here. I'll get it.

528
00:40:31,262 --> 00:40:33,764
-Just wait here, okay?
-Okay.

529
00:40:43,023 --> 00:40:44,066
Diego.

530
00:40:45,067 --> 00:40:47,445
[romantic music playing]

531
00:40:47,528 --> 00:40:49,864
Ivy, I just want to make sure
that you're safe.

532
00:40:50,781 --> 00:40:52,658
I understand that.

533
00:40:52,741 --> 00:40:53,826
But let me reiterate that

534
00:40:53,909 --> 00:40:56,245
I won't do anything that'll get me killed.

535
00:40:56,871 --> 00:40:58,581
I can protect myself.

536
00:40:58,664 --> 00:41:01,959
If you need me, you know where to find me.

537
00:41:04,670 --> 00:41:07,298
Thanks. You should go. Take care.

538
00:41:09,884 --> 00:41:11,177
Ivy, be careful.

539
00:41:15,306 --> 00:41:22,104
[unsettling music playing]

540
00:41:27,276 --> 00:41:29,778
[thunder rumbling]

541
00:41:29,862 --> 00:41:31,989
Oh, dear! Here we go again.

542
00:41:32,072 --> 00:41:36,160
We haven't even recovered yet,
but here comes another storm!

543
00:41:36,243 --> 00:41:38,954
-Give Dolfo some of that too.
-Thank you.

544
00:41:39,914 --> 00:41:43,167
-Miss Camia, have some juice.
-Thank you, Nimfa.

545
00:41:44,126 --> 00:41:46,754
That was a very beautiful speech.

546
00:41:47,254 --> 00:41:50,341
You're my idol! You're so inspiring.

547
00:41:51,008 --> 00:41:52,635
Thanks for all your help.

548
00:41:54,637 --> 00:41:55,804
[sighs]

549
00:41:55,888 --> 00:41:57,348
The truth is…

550
00:41:58,307 --> 00:42:00,851
my family is suffering
under the Ardientes too.

551
00:42:01,477 --> 00:42:02,978
That's why I'm doing this.

552
00:42:05,564 --> 00:42:07,983
Do you have any available jobs for me?

553
00:42:08,192 --> 00:42:10,528
I can work for free as a volunteer.

554
00:42:11,070 --> 00:42:12,363
Well…

555
00:42:12,446 --> 00:42:15,241
Nimfa, your help with
Diego's campaign is enough.

556
00:42:17,535 --> 00:42:20,496
[thunder rumbling]

557
00:42:24,375 --> 00:42:25,334
Mm…

558
00:42:25,417 --> 00:42:26,293
This is delicious.

559
00:42:26,877 --> 00:42:28,963
Thank you. I made it myself.

560
00:42:29,505 --> 00:42:31,674
You know, this is my daughter's favorite.

561
00:42:31,757 --> 00:42:32,841
Her name is Lily.

562
00:42:33,801 --> 00:42:35,052
Really?

563
00:42:35,135 --> 00:42:36,387
Where is she?

564
00:42:36,971 --> 00:42:41,559
[somber music playing]

565
00:42:42,268 --> 00:42:43,435
She's gone.

566
00:42:45,104 --> 00:42:46,105
Oh.

567
00:42:46,522 --> 00:42:47,856
Is she dead?

568
00:42:47,940 --> 00:42:52,027
[somber music playing]

569
00:42:57,866 --> 00:42:58,867
Miss Camia…

570
00:43:00,327 --> 00:43:01,495
Don't worry.

571
00:43:02,538 --> 00:43:04,623
Even if your daughter is gone…

572
00:43:05,583 --> 00:43:07,084
we'll always be here.

573
00:43:07,960 --> 00:43:09,253
We support you.

574
00:43:16,969 --> 00:43:18,804
-Let's eat more fritters.
-Okay.

575
00:43:18,887 --> 00:43:19,930
[both chuckling]

576
00:43:20,014 --> 00:43:22,766
-It's so delicious.
-Thank you.

577
00:43:35,696 --> 00:43:36,739
Congressman.

578
00:43:37,781 --> 00:43:38,991
Who's that from?

579
00:43:40,284 --> 00:43:41,493
It's from a certain Jaguar.

580
00:43:41,869 --> 00:43:44,371
They want to enter the
gambling scene here in Ardiente.

581
00:43:44,455 --> 00:43:46,957
You brought me this
without even checking it?!

582
00:43:47,625 --> 00:43:50,669
What if it's a bomb, and it kills us all?

583
00:43:55,049 --> 00:43:56,091
Jaguar?

584
00:43:57,134 --> 00:43:59,720
I've never heard that name before.

585
00:43:59,803 --> 00:44:01,263
Probably a newcomer.

586
00:44:02,765 --> 00:44:04,183
A newcomer?

587
00:44:04,266 --> 00:44:07,102
Why don't they come here and face me?

588
00:44:07,436 --> 00:44:09,396
Congressman, I asked them about that too,

589
00:44:09,480 --> 00:44:11,815
but they said it's not the right time.

590
00:44:12,524 --> 00:44:13,734
What an arrogant.

591
00:44:13,817 --> 00:44:16,195
Open it. Find out what it is.

592
00:44:17,571 --> 00:44:23,577
[unsettling music playing]

593
00:44:39,176 --> 00:44:40,928
Take that away and burn it.

594
00:44:41,261 --> 00:44:42,513
As you wish, Congressman.

595
00:44:47,518 --> 00:44:50,896
<i>This newcomer has some nerve.</i>

596
00:44:50,979 --> 00:44:54,650
<i>Kittens aren't welcome in my business.</i>

597
00:44:55,150 --> 00:45:01,740
<i>Only wild animals can mingle</i>
<i>with the Ardientes.</i>

598
00:45:01,824 --> 00:45:06,161
[unsettling music playing]

599
00:45:35,065 --> 00:45:36,150
Jaguar.

600
00:45:36,775 --> 00:45:38,902
The congressman did not accept your gifts.

601
00:45:47,744 --> 00:45:49,872
Get ready. We have a mission.

602
00:45:56,295 --> 00:45:58,297
[mahjong tiles shuffling]

603
00:46:05,971 --> 00:46:08,765
[poker chips rattling]

604
00:46:12,561 --> 00:46:13,645
[man] Who are you?

605
00:46:13,729 --> 00:46:15,105
What do you want?

606
00:46:21,737 --> 00:46:22,946
Is this a joke?

607
00:46:23,030 --> 00:46:24,698
-Who's your stupid mascot?
-[laughing]

608
00:46:24,781 --> 00:46:26,074
[grunts]

609
00:46:27,743 --> 00:46:29,328
[gunshots]

610
00:46:29,870 --> 00:46:31,288
[screams]

611
00:46:33,832 --> 00:46:35,334
Tell your boss…

612
00:46:36,543 --> 00:46:39,129
that we own this gambling den now.

613
00:46:39,213 --> 00:46:40,088
What?!

614
00:46:40,172 --> 00:46:41,882
Do you know who my boss is?

615
00:46:41,965 --> 00:46:44,301
Congressman Julio Ardiente.

616
00:46:44,384 --> 00:46:47,638
He owns this gambling den,
so if you've got a brain,

617
00:46:47,721 --> 00:46:49,014
you wouldn't go against him.

618
00:46:50,224 --> 00:46:51,266
[gunshot]

619
00:46:51,642 --> 00:46:52,768
[gunshot]

620
00:46:53,143 --> 00:46:54,728
Who wants to be next?

621
00:46:56,605 --> 00:46:58,398
Tell the congressman…

622
00:46:59,191 --> 00:47:00,734
that the Jaguar is here…

623
00:47:01,401 --> 00:47:04,780
and he will rule Poblacion Ardiente.

624
00:47:04,863 --> 00:47:09,243
[ominous music playing]

625
00:47:19,294 --> 00:47:22,130
Arnaldo, I couldn't find your painkillers.

626
00:47:26,843 --> 00:47:27,803
[sighs]

627
00:47:27,886 --> 00:47:28,929
It's here.

628
00:47:31,014 --> 00:47:33,016
That's good. How's your leg?

629
00:47:35,227 --> 00:47:37,229
Actually, I feel a lot better.

630
00:47:38,063 --> 00:47:42,276
Especially now that everything
is finally clear to me.

631
00:47:45,612 --> 00:47:47,447
What do you mean?

632
00:47:49,116 --> 00:47:50,534
I saw Diego.

633
00:47:54,037 --> 00:47:54,955
So…

634
00:47:55,497 --> 00:47:56,873
What is he doing here?

635
00:48:00,419 --> 00:48:02,045
-I don't know.
-Enough!

636
00:48:03,964 --> 00:48:04,881
Enough.

637
00:48:05,382 --> 00:48:08,218
-You're toying with me.
-Of course not! No!

638
00:48:08,302 --> 00:48:09,845
What's going on between you two?

639
00:48:10,220 --> 00:48:11,930
Nothing, Arnaldo.

640
00:48:12,472 --> 00:48:13,557
Nothing.

641
00:48:14,182 --> 00:48:15,434
Grandpa was right.

642
00:48:16,685 --> 00:48:17,811
Mom was right.

643
00:48:18,478 --> 00:48:21,773
-Arnaldo, listen to me.
-No.

644
00:48:23,191 --> 00:48:25,277
I'm done playing your games.

645
00:48:26,570 --> 00:48:27,654
I'm done.

646
00:48:27,738 --> 00:48:31,783
[unsettling music playing]

647
00:48:32,409 --> 00:48:34,745
-Arnaldo! Arnaldo, wait!
-What?

648
00:48:34,828 --> 00:48:36,246
-What?!
-Listen to me.

649
00:48:36,330 --> 00:48:38,749
Give me one good reason
why I need to stay!

650
00:48:38,832 --> 00:48:40,083
Hmm?

651
00:48:40,959 --> 00:48:44,171
Please, give me one good reason
to trust you.

652
00:48:44,796 --> 00:48:48,717
[unsettling music playing]

653
00:48:49,635 --> 00:48:50,886
Arnaldo…

654
00:48:56,600 --> 00:48:57,684
I love you.

655
00:49:01,438 --> 00:49:02,481
Stay.

656
00:49:03,482 --> 00:49:04,858
Stay, Arnaldo.

657
00:49:05,275 --> 00:49:06,360
I love you.

658
00:49:07,361 --> 00:49:13,408
[unsettling music playing]

659
00:49:21,625 --> 00:49:23,960
<i>-For the Jaguar.</i>
<i>-Jaguar!</i>

660
00:49:24,044 --> 00:49:27,631
[Julio] <i>I have had many encounters</i>
<i>and many threats</i>

661
00:49:27,714 --> 00:49:29,132
<i>in my political career.</i>

662
00:49:29,216 --> 00:49:31,593
<i>But I'm telling you,</i>
<i>this group is different.</i>

663
00:49:31,677 --> 00:49:33,929
<i>This group is dangerous.</i>

664
00:49:34,971 --> 00:49:36,348
[gunshots]

665
00:49:38,475 --> 00:49:40,435
[gunshots]

666
00:49:43,855 --> 00:49:45,273
[Diego] <i>You're going to marry the man</i>

667
00:49:45,357 --> 00:49:46,775
<i>who might've killed Nanny Carlotta?</i>

668
00:49:46,858 --> 00:49:49,444
<i>I'll do everything I can to stop</i>
<i>your wedding with Arnaldo.</i>

669
00:49:50,320 --> 00:49:54,116
[theme music playing]
